# Local-dev secrets. Copy to `.dev.vars` (gitignored) and fill in real
# values — never commit the real file. Production secrets are set
# separately via the Cloudflare dashboard / `wrangler secret put <NAME>`,
# not from this file.

# Pexels API key (write-article skill only — read at authoring time when
# sourcing a cover image for a conceptual post; never shipped to the
# deployed Worker, since images are downloaded once and committed as
# static assets, not fetched at build or request time). Free key from
# https://www.pexels.com/api/.
PEXELS_API_KEY=your-pexels-api-key-here

# Cloudflare Workers AI credentials for scripts/generate-conceptual-cover.mjs
# (write-article skill's AI-generated-cover fallback, used only when no
# Pexels photo is a genuine fit for a conceptual post — see write-article
# §3). A separate concern from the CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN GitHub Actions
# secret that deploys the Worker: this one is used locally, at authoring
# time, to call the Workers AI REST API directly, never shipped to the
# deployed Worker. Needs the "Workers AI" permission (Read is sufficient
# for inference). Account ID is on any zone's Overview page in the
# Cloudflare dashboard.
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=your-cloudflare-api-token-here
CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=your-cloudflare-account-id-here
